{"lines": ["How is Hitler connected to Kermit the Frog?", "In nineteen thirty-eight, British prime minister Neville Chamberlain signed the Munich Agreement with Hitler, hoping to avoid war.", "In nineteen forty, Chamberlain's fellow Conservative, Winston Churchill, replaced him as prime minister.", "On Victory in Europe Day, nineteen forty-five, Churchill stood on the palace balcony beside young Princess Elizabeth.", "In two thousand nine, Queen Elizabeth the Second welcomed Barack and Michelle Obama to Buckingham Palace.", "And in twenty fourteen, Michelle Obama introduced Kermit the Frog at a White House screening of Muppets Most Wanted.", "How is Adolf Hitler connected to Grug?", "In October nineteen forty, Hitler met Spain's dictator Francisco Franco at Hendaye, trying to pull Spain into the war.", "Spain stayed out, and in nineteen fifty-nine Franco welcomed President Dwight Eisenhower to Madrid.", "Eisenhower's vice president for eight years was a young senator named Richard Nixon.", "In December nineteen seventy, Elvis Presley showed up at the White House asking President Nixon for a narcotics badge.", "In nineteen sixty-eight, Elvis posed with his newborn daughter, Lisa Marie.", "In two thousand one, Lisa Marie sat beside Nicolas Cage at the Capitol, and the next year they married.", "And Grug, the caveman dad of The Croods, is voiced by Nicolas Cage.", "How is Joseph Stalin connected to Elmo?", "In nineteen forty-five, Joseph Stalin sat beside Winston Churchill at Yalta to plan the end of World War Two.", "In February nineteen fifty-three, Prime Minister Churchill greeted the new Queen, Elizabeth the Second, and her children.", "In May two thousand seven, on a state visit to America, the Queen toured a Washington children's hospital with Laura Bush.", "And that same month, Laura Bush posed with Elmo at a Sesame Street benefit dinner in New York."], "heard": [["How", 0.0, 0.36], ["is", 0.36, 0.58], ["Hitler", 0.58, 0.76], ["connected", 0.76, 1.28], ["to", 1.